5417 true] [17592186427208 1072 #uuid "4ab049c7-8771-5b28-bd3b-011a826d75ca" 13194139534596 17592186045417 true] [17592186427208 1074 "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=P(X=x\\,|\\,Y=y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the following set of conditional probabilities:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)=P(X=x\\,|\\,Y=2)\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=x\\,|\\,Y=2)=\\frac{P(X=x,Y=2)}{P(Y=2)}=\\frac{f(x,2)}{{f}_{Y}(2)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distributions for $X$ and $Y$ correspond to the row and column totals, respectively. So, let's compute these:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.6$ | $0.4$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, for $x\\in \\{0,2,4\\},$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0\\,|\\,Y=2) & =\\frac{f(0,2)}{{f}_{Y}(2)}=\\frac{0.1}{0.4}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(X=2\\,|\\,Y=2) & =\\frac{f(2,2)}{{f}_{Y}(2)}=\\frac{0.2}{0.4}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ P(X=4\\,|\\,Y=2) & =\\frac{f(4,2)}{{f}_{Y}(2)}=\\frac{0.1}{0.4}=\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the conditional probability mass function can be represented by the following table:   \n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |" 13194139534596 17592186045417 true] [17592186427209 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427204 13194139534596 17592186045417 true] [17592186427209 1069 "q-142862" 13194139534596 17592186045417 true] [17592186427209 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534596 17592186045417 true] [17592186427209 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ | $Y=7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ |\n\nCompute $P(1<Y<7\\,|\\,X=2)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." 13194139534596 17592186045417 true] [17592186427209 1072 #uuid "5f05ade6-f4a6-518d-b188-3b387ae00a2d" 13194139534596 17592186045417 true] [17592186427209 1074 "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required conditional probability is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<Y<7\\,|\\,X=2) & =\\frac{P((1<Y<7),X=2)}{P(X=2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=2,(1<Y<7))}{P(X=2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=2,Y=3)+P(X=2,Y=5)}{P(X=2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(2,3)+f(2,5)}{{f}_{X}(2)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(2) & =f(2,1)+f(2,3)+f(2,5)+f(2,7) \\\\  & =0+0.05+0.05+0.1 \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(2,3)=0.05$ and $f(2,5)=0.05.$ \n\nFinally, substituting our values into our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<Y<7\\,|\\,X=2) & =\\frac{f(2,3)+f(2,5)}{{f}_{X}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.05+0.05}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.1}{0.2} \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534596 17592186045417 true] [17592186427210 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427203 13194139534596 17592186045417 true] [17592186427210 1069 "q-142884" 13194139534596 17592186045417 true] [17592186427210 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534596 17592186045417 true] [17592186427210 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{18}$ | $\\frac{1}{18}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{18}$ |\n\nCompute $P(Y=0\\,|\\,X=3)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." 13194139534596 17592186045417 true] [17592186427210 1072 #uuid "dd1f8e38-c35e-55be-bdf0-b84dac107dde" 13194139534596 17592186045417 true] [17592186427210 1074 "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required probability is given by\n\n$$\nP(Y=0\\,|\\,X=3)=\\frac{P(X=3,Y=0)}{P(X=3)}=\\frac{f(3,0)}{{f}_{X}(3)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(3) & =f(3,0)+f(3,1)+f(3,2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{18}+\\frac{2}{18}+\\frac{1}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(3,0)=\\frac{1}{9}.$ \n\nFinally, substituting ${f}_{X}(3)=\\frac{5}{18}$ and $f(3,0)=\\frac{1}{9}$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=0\\,|\\,X=3) & =\\frac{f(3,0)}{{f}_{X}(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{9})}{(\\frac{5}{18})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534596 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-02d64482-a157-593b-a0d1-db5b6744fac2" 17592186427178 "answer-06f6b37e-e1c4-56fe-af0d-d05220252493" 17592186427179 "answer-10a5a9d4-3a44-5769-9f6b-52e2cb75f730" 17592186427180 "answer-2f47c227-7ea9-5c71-8c0a-c370a8c2740e" 17592186427181 "answer-33614170-1060-5986-98ed-e0d47798ec54" 17592186427182 "answer-4329cac3-a508-561d-92e3-75791b4b2a53" 17592186427183 "answer-4bcd313c-8a81-5a91-877f-2970fdc8ac87" 17592186427184 "answer-558ce6b2-7ed9-580c-a0dc-2f742abaac0a" 17592186427185 "answer-5da297a0-8c40-5743-92dd-89674c59b084" 17592186427186 "answer-6429f8f1-6f22-5c87-b7fa-2aa976d2cf28" 17592186427187 "answer-778478e6-34f7-5241-9c21-a6104ba3033d" 17592186427188 "answer-7df7cc62-41f2-5b67-8003-b3f2f792fe42" 17592186427189 "answer-9258e615-4af2-514e-a284-343d0ce33226" 